<title>RUSSIA: Russia's UES utility rises over 11 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia's UES utility rises over 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in national power grid owner and utility RAO UES had risen 11.5 percent by 1120 GMT to $0.2180 from $0.1955 at Monday's close on the Russian Trading System (RTS).</p>
<p>One of Russia's most liquid stocks and an indicator of market sentiment, RAO Yedinaya Energeticheskaya Sistema Rossii broke the 20 cent barrier on Tuesday morning and was the share turnover leader with over 16 million shares changing hands.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
